WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.187
Let's create a neighborhood decorating contest.

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:08.818
With Quick start, you will have a live contest, with its own link and QR code, in a few minutes.

00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:14.159
I will explain what every screen is for as we go, so you always know what you are choosing.

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:15.611
We will start on the map.

00:00:16.514 --> 00:00:18.263
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:20.414 --> 00:00:22.931
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:25.709
Then tap Allow.

00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:29.775
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:33.947
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:40.539
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:45.613
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:46.808
See the three dots?

00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:51.111
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:51.649
Tap them.

00:00:53.343 --> 00:00:54.751
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:56.535 --> 00:01:00.631
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own house.

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:02.693
This is the Add page.

00:01:02.693 --> 00:01:04.052
It has three choices.

00:01:04.052 --> 00:01:07.265
An event, like a tree lighting or a holiday parade.

00:01:07.265 --> 00:01:12.580
A contest, where neighbors enter their homes, and the community votes for a favorite.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.669
Or a lighting display, to show off your own house.

00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:19.124
We are creating a contest, so tap A contest.

00:01:21.282 --> 00:01:22.295
First, the name.

00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:28.490
This is the title everyone sees, on the contest page, on the map, and in the emails your neighbors get.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.613
Something simple and local works best, like your street or neighborhood, and the year.

00:01:34.313 --> 00:01:37.705
I will type Oak Hill Holiday Lights 2026.

00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:38.836
Then tap Next.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.161
Next, who is running it, and where.

00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:44.878
Type the name of your group.

00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:50.502
It can be a city, a school, an H O A, a club, a business, or just your neighbors on one street.

00:01:51.201 --> 00:01:53.261
Then pick the city the homes are in.

00:01:53.261 --> 00:01:56.546
That is how your contest shows up for the right neighbors.

00:01:56.546 --> 00:01:57.047
Tap Next.

00:01:58.847 --> 00:02:00.508
This is the welcome message.

00:02:00.508 --> 00:02:06.292
Neighbors read it before they decide to enter, so it is your chance to say what the contest is about.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.284
We already wrote a friendly one for you.

00:02:09.284 --> 00:02:13.252
You can keep it as it is, or change a few words so it sounds like you.

00:02:13.252 --> 00:02:13.755
Tap Next.

00:02:15.553 --> 00:02:16.950
A website is optional.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.868
If your group has one, add it here, and people can see who is behind the contest.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:26.961
Your contest goes live right away either way, so it is fine to skip this.

00:02:26.961 --> 00:02:27.495
Tap Next.

00:02:29.293 --> 00:02:30.100
Now the dates.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.015
There are three.

00:02:31.015 --> 00:02:32.791
The last day neighbors can enter.

00:02:33.492 --> 00:02:34.817
The day voting starts.

00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:36.201
And the day voting ends.

00:02:37.822 --> 00:02:41.696
Entries and voting open and close on these dates by themselves.

00:02:41.696 --> 00:02:44.904
We filled in typical dates, so you can just tap Next.

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:49.182
You can change any of them later, from your dashboard.

00:02:50.081 --> 00:02:52.916
This is the big choice, how the rules are set up.

00:02:52.916 --> 00:02:56.545
Quick start is the recommended one, and it is what we are using.

00:02:57.245 --> 00:03:02.659
It turns on public voting, where anyone with an account gets one vote in each category.

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:09.427
It gives you four voting categories: Best Overall, Most Creative, Best Lights and Music, and Best Traditional.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.334
It lets you approve every entry before it reaches the map.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.667
And it writes your official rules for you.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.728
Everything can still be changed later.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:23.842
If you would rather choose judges, prizes, or your own categories, pick Customize everything.

00:03:23.842 --> 00:03:25.684
We cover that in the next video.

00:03:26.384 --> 00:03:28.923
For now, choose Quick start, then tap Next.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:33.197
The last screen is the review.

00:03:33.197 --> 00:03:38.691
It lists everything you chose: the name, who runs it, the dates, the categories, and who can vote.

00:03:39.391 --> 00:03:42.311
If something is not right, tap Edit next to it.

00:03:42.311 --> 00:03:45.231
Nothing is public until you tap Create contest.

00:03:45.231 --> 00:03:47.604
When you are happy, tap Create contest.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.417
That is it.

00:03:50.417 --> 00:03:51.769
Your contest is live.

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:54.103
This page explains what happens next.

00:03:54.103 --> 00:03:56.376
You share your link or your QR code.

00:03:56.376 --> 00:03:58.157
Neighbors enter their homes.

00:03:58.157 --> 00:04:01.351
You look over each entry before it goes on the map.

00:04:01.351 --> 00:04:06.142
Then the community votes, on the dates you set, and you announce the winners.

00:04:06.142 --> 00:04:07.494
Tap Open my dashboard.

00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:10.758
This is your dashboard.

00:04:10.758 --> 00:04:12.580
It is where you run the contest.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.604
Up here are the numbers that matter: your entries, the ones waiting for you, and the votes.

00:04:18.306 --> 00:04:23.837
And here is your link, and your QR code, ready to paste into a message, or print for a flyer.

00:04:23.837 --> 00:04:25.837
We will cover sharing in a moment.

00:04:27.038 --> 00:04:29.641
Next up: Create a contest with Customize.
